CatCup is licensed AGPL-3.0 by its own choice. The character card, chat,
world info and preset formats it reads and writes are the tavern ecosystem's
shared standard, implemented here from the specifications.

**No file in this repository is another project's code.** Everything that was
once adapted from another client has been rewritten: the behaviour was taken
from the documentation, and the implementation is this project's. What follows is
what that rewrite could not remove — one data file and one algorithm whose
outputs have to stay identical to what existing files already contain.

Third-party material included or depended on:

1. Claude tokenizer vocabulary
   apps/server/assets/tokenizers/claude.json
   Copied from SillyTavern's src/tokenizers/claude.json
   (https://github.com/SillyTavern/SillyTavern), Copyright (C) SillyTavern
   contributors, licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, v3.
   This is a byte-level BPE vocabulary — data rather than code. It is shipped
   verbatim because a token budget computed from anything else would disagree
   with what the same prompt costs in the client that produced the file.

2. cyrb53 string hash
   Copyright (C) 2018 bryc
   Public domain / MIT.
   Used as published by packages/compat-st/src/hash.ts. The hash is how a chat
   file stores its timed world info state, so the algorithm must match for
   imported chats to keep working.

3. @agnai/web-tokenizers
   https://github.com/mlc-ai/tokenizers-cpp
   Copyright (C) MLC AI
   Licensed under the Apache License, version 2.0.
   Runtime dependency used to load the Claude vocabulary.

4. js-tiktoken
   Licensed under the MIT License.
   Runtime dependency used for the OpenAI-family token counts.

5. Inter and Newsreader (web fonts)
   apps/web/public/fonts/{inter-latin,inter-latin-ext,newsreader-latin}.woff2
   Inter, Copyright (C) The Inter Project Authors (https://github.com/rsms/inter)
   Newsreader, Copyright (C) The Newsreader Project Authors
   (https://github.com/productiontype/Newsreader)
   Both licensed under the SIL Open Font License, version 1.1
   (https://openfontlicense.org). The font files are redistributed unmodified,
   as latin and latin-ext woff2 subsets, and are not sold on their own. The
   reserved font names are unchanged, which the OFL permits for unmodified
